<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/4th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siege of Pelium</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">335 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> · Also known as Battle of Pelium</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Siege of Pelium was fought in 335 BCE when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> attacked the Illyrian king Cleitus at the fortress of Pelion on the western border of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a>. The arrival of the Taulantian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glaukias">Glaukias</a> threatened to trap the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonian-empire">Macedonians</a>, but Alexander withdrew by a bold manoeuvre and then routed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illyrians">Illyrians</a> in a night attack. The victory secured his western frontier before he marched on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thebes-greece">Thebes</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/siege-of-pelium.jpg" alt="Siege of Pelium" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dodge, Theodore Ayrault, 1842-1909 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Plain_of_Pelium.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
